🟠 **bug** (high)

The mismatch guard fails open. `vscode.window.showWarningMessage` resolves to `undefined` when the user dismisses the notification (Esc / close button / clicking outside), and the code only aborts when the result is exactly the string `"Cancel"`. Any dismissed or unhandled prompt therefore falls through to `if (token) { ... }` and stores the token even though the state did not match the stored nonce — exactly the untrusted-callback scenario this check is supposed to stop. Previously the mismatch path returned unconditionally, so this is a regression introduced by the PR.

**建议**: Invert the condition to an explicit allow-list, so only a deliberate "Store" click proceeds:

```ts
if (authService.authNonce !== state) {
    const userConfirmation = await vscode.window.showWarningMessage(
        `The authentication response could not be verified. Store the token returned from ${uri.path}?`,
        { modal: true },
        "Store",
    )
    if (userConfirmation !== "Store") {
        console.log("User declined to continue with auth callback due to state mismatch")
        return
    }
}
```
